# Phase 5 L-U1: every OSC 7501 report on the wire, state by state, on fx and
# xfx. Startup idle; a turn held mid-stream (working), then done; a second
# turn (done again); a 400 (error); a command in ask mode (blocked:permission,
# its label in `msg`), answered once; a question (blocked:question, its text
# in `msg`), answered; and the planned exit's restore (clear). The tools are
# each product's own -- fx's `shell` is xfx's `terminal` -- so the command's
# label differs by its tool's name and nothing else. Wire only: each `wire`
# is every byte written so far.
fx: gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-states-fx.json
xfx: gateway p5-lifecycle-osc-states-xfx.json
fx: seed p5-lifecycle-ask-settings.json
fx: env FX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_PERMISSION_MODE=ask
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 4
wire w00-start
type first question
key Enter
held
wire w01-working
release
wait 3
wire w02-done
type second question
key Enter
wait 2.5
wire w03-done2
type third question
key Enter
wait 3
wire w04-error
type run the command
key Enter
wait 3
wire w05-permission
key 1
wait 3
wire w06-after-permission
type ask me
key Enter
wait 3
wire w07-question
key 1
wait 3
wire w08-after-question
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 2
wire w09-exit
